0..83 Comment "//! An eliminator that writes its answer, `if c -> C { … }` or `case e -> C { …"
84..160 Comment "//! }`, answers it wherever it stands: the case is ascribed the answer, so a"
161..238 Comment "//! computation a `run` binds, which states no type, synthesises it, and each"
239..318 Comment "//! arm is checked against it. The rule is the annotation rule of bidirectional"
319..391 Comment "//! typing [Dunfield-2019-bidirectional_typing], § 3: an annotated term"
392..423 Comment "//! synthesises its annotation."
424..427 Comment "//!"
428..444 Comment "//! - see: #2089"
